# =====================================================================
# Jackie Lives — .gitignore for the PUBLIC repo
# Goal: publish only SOURCE (code, configs, docs, tools), never the
# copyrighted game audio or large downloaded binaries.
# =====================================================================

# --- COPYRIGHTED GAME AUDIO (CDPR) — must NOT be redistributed --------
# Jackie's voice lines scraped from SoundDB / converted for Audioware.
# These are regenerated locally by tools/scrape_jackie.py + tools/convert_audio.py.
audioware/JackieLives/*.ogg
audioware/JackieLives/*.wav
audioware/JackieLives/*.wem
tools/voice-tagger/audio/
**/recorded_lines.json

# --- COPYRIGHTED DIALOGUE TRANSCRIPTS (CDPR) -------------------------
# Full verbatim dumps of all 777 of Jackie's lines (text). Regenerated by the
# scraper / convert script. lines.sample.json (a tiny example) IS kept.
tools/voice-tagger/lines.json
audioware/JackieLives/index.json

# --- Local Claude Code settings (personal, not shared) ---------------
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- Large downloaded binaries (regenerable, not source) -------------
# portable ffmpeg (~211MB, downloaded by tools/convert_audio.py)
tools/ffmpeg/
tools/ffmpeg.zip

# --- Private / local-only --------------------------------------------
# Claude Code chat history + state (per CLAUDE.md, large + private)
**/documents/Claude_chat_history.md
**/documents/.chat_history_state.json
**/Claude_chat_history.md

# --- Python ----------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# --- OS / editors ----------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# --- Logs / temp -----------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.tmp

# --- Local-only images (Nexus page art / refs; not source) -----------
jackie.png
mod_thumbnail.png
Jackies_noodles.jpg

# --- Tools (not source; downloaded locally) --------------------------
WolvenKit-*/
WolvenKit*.zip

# --- Other people's mods, kept locally ONLY to read ------------------
# They live at ../reference_mods/ (outside every repo) — this line is a defensive
# net in case a copy is ever moved inside. NEVER commit or republish them: they are
# other authors' work, and their .archive files contain CDPR assets. See ../GROUND_RULES.md.
reference_mods/

# --- Built game archives (binary assets; keep repo source-only) ------
*.archive
# ...EXCEPT our own. JackieLives.archive is the generated voiceover MAP (a few KB of JSON,
# no audio, nothing of CDPR's to redistribute), and package_nexus.sh cannot build a zip
# without it — so ignoring it meant a fresh clone could not produce a release at all, while
# NCLives and NCLucy have always tracked theirs. The blanket rule above still covers every
# third-party and reference archive, which is what it was written for.
!archive/pc/mod/JackieLives.archive
!staging/archive/pc/mod/JackieLives.archive

# COPYRIGHTED transcripts of CDPR VO (like index.json) — never commit
audioware/JackieLives/transcripts.json
audioware/JackieLives/transcripts.txt

# rebuild_bank_yml.py backup of the previous manifest
audioware/JackieLives/*.yml.bak

# R console history (junk)
.Rhistory

# Extracted CDPR quest-graph JSON (datamining artifact, do not redistribute)
docs/research/q005_raw/
docs/research/q101_raw/
# Raw base-game mourning/reaction scene dumps (~222MB of CDPR .scene JSON; local authoring reference only)
docs/mounring_scenes/
# Raw q005 heist scene tree (~141MB of CDPR .scene/.anims/.particle JSON; source for the mix-signpost find)
docs/Heist_scene_tree_base/

# luac bytecode dumps (luac -l without -p writes these)
luac.out

# dialogue editor: local .lua backups (never committed)
tools/dialogue-editor/backups/

# packaged Nexus zips (build output — rebuild with tools/package_nexus.sh)
dist/

# --- Video project files + raw footage (large, not mod source) --------
*.kdenlive
gameplay_showcase1/
# rotated debug log (the live one is covered by *.log)
*.log.prev

# --- THE LINE LIBRARY (CDPR's subtitle text, verbatim) ----------------
# Built by tools/build_line_library.py from whoever's own install. It is CDPR's text, so it is
# theirs, not ours: never committed, never shipped (GROUND_RULES: game assets are not
# redistributable). Regenerating it on another machine takes ~100 s, which is cheaper than the
# licence question. tools/voicetags.json IS committed — that is nothing but voicetag numbers
# and character names. vo_library/v_index.json is derived from it and is equally CDPR's.
vo_library/
